WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.640
 Welcome to Delicious Revolution, a show about food, culture, and place. I'm Chelsea Wills.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:21.240
 In this fifth season, we're speaking with visionary chefs, gardeners, farmers, organizers, artists, and scientists about migrations of all kinds.

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:31.760
 We'll hear about food and the experience of leaving home and in finding new ones, of decolonizing food traditions, and tracing recipes through the movements of diaspora.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.610
 Delicious Revolution is made by Devon Samson and Chelsea Wills.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:40.820
 You can subscribe to the show on Apple Podcasts, or wherever you get your podcasts.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:48.620
 And you can find all of our episodes, along with pictures and more, on the website deliciousrevolutionshow.com.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:01:01.870
 The People's Kitchen Collective works at the intersection of art and activism as a food-centered political education project and cooperative business.

00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:08.100
 Based in Oakland, California, their creative practices reflect the diverse histories and backgrounds of collective members

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.100
 Sita Kuratomi Baumik, Jocelyn Jackson, and Saqib Kavav.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.540
 Written in their families' recipes are maps of migrations and the stories of resilience.

00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:22.530
 It is from their foundation that they create immersive experiences that celebrate centuries of shared struggle.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:27.530
 Collectively cooking and sharing food is sanctified and celebrated community work in many cultures.

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:34.970
 With passage of time, systems of imperialism, including capitalism and gentrification, have turned cooking into an inaccessible burden.

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:40.970
 In response to this inequality, PKC has been creating accessible, healthy, and loving food spaces since 2007.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:49.970
 Active in Oakland since 2011, they've been committed to using local and organic ingredients whenever possible and sharing meals with as many people as they can.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:56.970
 The goal of the People's Kitchen Collective is not only to fill stomachs, but to nourish souls, feed minds, and fuel movement.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:05.970
 In this episode, PKC talks with Chelsea about nourishing a radical, beloved community and feeding movements from the farm to the kitchen to the table to the street.

